{title: Get up and walk}
{subtitle: John 5:1–15}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [F] | [Eb] |
| [Dm] | [Cm] | [Gm] | [Eb] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
By the [Gm]Sheep Gate in Jerusalem [Dm]stands a pool
[Cm]Called Bethesda where the sick all [Bb]are
Five [Cm]covered colonnades hold the [Gm]crowd
Blind and lame and [F]paralyzed remain
[Eb]Waiting for the water to be [F]stirred
An [Gm]angel comes to stir the [Dm]waves
The [Eb]first to step in after the [Bb]stir
Is [Cm]healed of whatever [Gm]illness held him [Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]One man there had been an in[Dm]valid
For [Cm]thir-ty-eight long years he [Bb]lay
[Cm]Jesus saw him lying there be[Gm]low
And asked if he desi[F]red to be well
The [Eb]sick man answered with a [F]sigh
[Gm]I have no one to help me [Dm]in
While [Eb]I am on my way to the [Bb]pool
[Cm]Someone else goes down ahead [Gm]of me [Eb][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Gm]Jesus said to him in [Dm]that hour
[Eb]Get up and pick up your [Bb]mat
And [Cm]walk with me this very day
[Gm]At once the man was made well
He [Eb]picked up his mat and be[F]gan to walk
[Gm]Now that day was a [Dm]Sabbath
[Eb]The Jews said it is not per[Bb]mitted
To [Cm]carry your mat on this [Gm]holy day [Eb][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
But he [Gm]answered the man who made me [Dm]well
[Cm]Told me to pick it up and [Bb]walk
[Cm]Who is the man who told you [Gm]so
They asked him in the [F]crowd
But the [Eb]man who had been healed did not [F]know
[Gm]Jesus had slipped away from the [Dm]place
Later [Eb]Jesus found him in the tem[Bb]ple
And [Cm]spoke to him with [Gm]gentle [Eb]care
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Cm]Sin no more or [Gm]something worse may happen
{end_of_verse}
